<section class="feat" id="features">
  <div class="kicker">Features</div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:12px">Four jobs. One binary underneath.</h2>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col orient"><div class="verb">Orient</div><div class="job">Where things are, in seconds, for an agent with no memory of the last hour.</div><ul>
      <li><div><b>Structure map</b><span>Tree with hubs called out, budgeted to fit a session-start hook.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Skyline</b><span>Every language a building. Animated in the terminal.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>find</b><span>Ranked by path and symbol, every hit tagged with its importer count.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Dependency flow</b><span>Imports resolved through go.mod, cargo metadata, package exports, tsconfig, pubspec.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Mermaid export</b><span>The graph around a change, pasted into a PR or a wiki.</span></div><span class="st soon">soon</span></li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="col protect"><div class="verb">Protect</div><div class="job">Know what breaks before the edit, and know when the answer is incomplete.</div><ul>
      <li><div><b>Blast radius</b><span>Who imports this file, hub or not, asked before the edit.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Hook warnings</b><span>Pre-edit and prompt-submit hooks flag hub files to Claude Code and Codex.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Coverage contract</b><span>complete, partial, unavailable on every answer, with provenance.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Self-healing config</b><span>Any command writes a tuned config when one is missing.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Hub warnings in the IDE</b><span>Same fact, at the moment a human opens the file.</span></div><span class="st soon">soon</span></li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="col coord"><div class="verb">Coordinate</div><div class="job">Many agents, one repo, and a merge order that does not break main.</div><ul>
      <li><div><b>collide</b><span>Rank open PRs by the files they share, weighted by importers.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>codemap CI</b><span>Pair-build the predicted pairs, red check and comment on the PR in 16 seconds.</span></div><span class="st team">team</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Merge order</b><span>Land in this order; these two cannot both land as-is.</span></div><span class="st team">team</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Calibration log</b><span>Every pair build recorded so the hit rate is measured on your repo, not guessed.</span></div><span class="st team">team</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Handoff</b><span>A layered artifact so a second agent resumes where the first stopped.</span></div><span class="st free">free</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Edit-time awareness</b><span>"Another open PR is already in this file" before the agent edits.</span></div><span class="st soon">soon</span></li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="col report"><div class="verb">Report</div><div class="job">What the fleet did while you slept, in the place you already read.</div><ul>
      <li><div><b>Morning ledger</b><span>Per repo: opened, merged, hub touches, collisions, in Slack at 9am.</span></div><span class="st team">team</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Session attribution</b><span>PRs grouped by the agent session that wrote them.</span></div><span class="st team">team</span></li>
      <li><div><b>The brief</b><span>One page per repo in Linear, Jira and Confluence.</span></div><span class="st preview">preview</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Ask in plain words</b><span>Do we use X, where is X, what changed, who depends on X, cited to path:line.</span></div><span class="st preview">preview</span></li>
      <li><div><b>Territory map</b><span>Assign agents non-overlapping areas on a FigJam or Miro board.</span></div><span class="st soon">soon</span></li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:26px;font-size:.92em;max-width:70ch">Peers, so you can pick by what you need: <a href="https://github.com/Ataraxy-Labs/sem">sem</a> does symbol-level impact analysis. <a href="https://github.com/oraios/serena">serena</a> and <a href="https://github.com/DeusData/codebase-memory-mcp">codebase-memory-mcp</a> are broader MCP servers. codemap resolves imports through each ecosystem's real rules and says when it does not know.</p>
</section>

<section class="contract grid">
  <div class="txt">
    <div class="kicker">The coverage contract</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:12px">A partial graph never reads as a complete one.</h2>
    <p>A timed-out scan returns an empty result with provenance, not a silent empty graph and not a hard error. An agent can tell "nothing imports this" apart from "I couldn't tell". That is the difference between a safe refactor and a Friday incident.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="code"><div class="term"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="t">codemap --json --deps . | jq .coverage</span></div><pre>&#123;
  <span class="k">"status"</span>: <span class="s">"partial"</span>,
  <span class="k">"sources"</span>: [
    &#123; <span class="k">"name"</span>: "ast-grep",      <span class="k">"status"</span>: <span class="g">"authoritative"</span> &#125;,
    &#123; <span class="k">"name"</span>: "cargo-metadata", <span class="k">"status"</span>: <span class="g">"authoritative"</span> &#125;,
    &#123; <span class="k">"name"</span>: "rust-cargo",     <span class="k">"status"</span>: <span class="s">"mixed"</span>,
      <span class="k">"detail"</span>: "macro-generated and conditional
                 path edges may be unresolved" &#125;
  ]
&#125;</pre></div><div class="cap">Versioned payload, schema_version codemap.analysis/v1.</div></div>
</section>

<section class="flow">
  <div class="kicker">From terminal to team</div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:12px">The same facts, three places.</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><div class="n">01</div><h3>In the terminal and the agent</h3><p>Structure, blast radius, find, diff, handoff. Hooks for Claude Code and Codex, MCP for anything else. Nothing phones home.</p><div class="tier">free · MIT</div></li>
    <li><div class="n">02</div><h3>In CI, on every PR</h3><p>CI builds every PR against main and never against its siblings. codemap CI pair-builds the open PRs that share hot files, posts the verdict on the PR, and turns the check red before either one lands. Runs on your runners in about 16 seconds.</p><div class="tier">team</div></li>
    <li><div class="n">03</div><h3>In Slack, Linear, Jira</h3><p>A morning ledger across every repo: what landed, what touched a hub, which open PRs are about to collide and in what order to merge them. Grouped by the agent session that did the work.</p><div class="tier">team</div></li>
  </ol>
</section>

